CORE
main.c
--pointer-check --strict-static-array --show-properties
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^Property read_dynamic.pointer_dereference.1:$
access is outside the exact static array size
^  \(signed __CPROVER_bitvector\[65\]\)\(signed long int\)i >= 0 && !\(\(signed __CPROVER_bitvector\[65\]\)\(signed long int\)i >= 4\)$
--
^Property read_known.pointer_dereference.
^Property read_dynamic.pointer_dereference.2:$
^warning: ignoring
--
Shows that --strict-static-array replaces a direct dynamic access with one
index-range property and eliminates known in-range accesses.
